Every build embeds the four files: the browser editor, the desktop app, the
command line and the Python package. A build that finds no installed Arial
(the browser, and Linux systems or containers without it) loads them and lists
them under the family names Arial and Liberation Sans, and outside the browser
also Helvetica when no Helvetica is installed. Liberation Sans has Arial's
character widths, which match Helvetica's, so drawings lay out as on macOS and
Windows. Where Arial is installed, the embedded files are not loaded. The font
files themselves are not changed; only the font database ReShiki builds in
memory gives them the extra names.
